cff-version: "1.2.0"
type: software

title: "Web Mining and Applied NLP 06: Clinical Fall-Risk NLP Pipeline"

authors:
  - family-names: Spornitz
    given-names: Beth

  - family-names: Case
    given-names: Denise M.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6165-7389"
    affiliation: "Northwest Missouri State University, USA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/BethSpornitz/nlp-06-nlp-pipeline-custom"
url: "https://BethSpornitz.github.io/nlp-06-nlp-pipeline-custom/"
license: MIT

abstract: |
  A reproducible natural language processing pipeline for analyzing
  vocabulary patterns in academic research on clinical fall-risk
  assessment. This project adapts the EVTAL pipeline developed by
  Denise M. Case and applies it to an academic paper on clinical
  fall-risk assessment. The custom analysis compares token
  frequencies and vocabulary diversity with and without stopword
  removal using Python, BeautifulSoup, Pandas, and spaCy.

